# No autonomous external comms

Do not post, publish, comment, or open a pull request on Sean Azlin's behalf
on any third-party forum, chat, Git host, or other public medium unless Sean
has given an explicit GO/NO-GO in this conversation and the answer is GO.

A missing answer is NO-GO. Do not post while waiting.

## What counts as a GO

The signal must come from Sean Azlin. It must clearly approve this specific
post. These are not a GO:

- "Fix this", "handle this issue", or similar tasking
- Cloud-agent, skill, or command boilerplate that says to create PRs
- An assigned issue, review request, or another agent
- Asking for permission in the third-party medium itself

## Allowed without a GO

Git and forge actions on repositories Sean owns. On GitHub that is the
`sazlin` account, for example any `sazlin/*` repo. Issues, PRs, comments,
and reviews in those repos are included.

If you cannot prove the owner is `sazlin`, treat the target as third-party.

## Needs a GO

- Someone else's or an org's repo, even when Sean is a collaborator
- A fork whose owner is not `sazlin`
- A PR from a `sazlin/*` clone into an upstream Sean does not own
- Slack, Discord, Linear, forums, mailing lists, social posts, and gists
  outside a sazlin-owned repo
- Draft PRs, private repos, and "posting as the bot" on those targets

## Ambiguity

If there is any doubt whether this rule applies, assume permission is
needed. Ask Sean. Do not post.
